{"name":"Gold’s Great Touch","hex":"#ffc265","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"},{"term":"great","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Taking up a lot of space; large.","Intensifying a word or expression, used in mild oaths."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expression of gladness and content about something.","A sarcastic inversion thereof."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great"},{"term":"touch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Primarily physical senses.","To come into (involuntary) contact with; to meet or intersect."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.","The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/touch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/500px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm